{"name":"Cuba Libre","hex":"#73383c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"libre","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Especially of the will: free, independent, unconstrained.","With very few limitations on distribution or the right to access the source code to create improved versions, but not necessarily free of charge. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A free (not enslaved) black person in a French- or Spanish-colonized area, especially New Orleans."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/libre"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cuba Libre (Gloria Estefan song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Cuba Libre\" is a 1998 song by American singer and songwriter Gloria Estefan. It was released as the third single from her eighth studio album, Gloria!. It is a dance-pop song which was included on the album in two versions: English and Spanish. The song is one of the three only Spanish-language tracks, alongside \"Oye\" and \"Corazón Prohibido\". It represents a homage to Estefan's homeland, Cuba. \"Cuba Libre\" was written and composed by Gloria Estefan, along with Emilio Estefan Jr. and Kike Santander."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d0/Gloria_Estefan_Cuba_Libre_Single.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba_Libre_(Gloria_Estefan_song)"},{"title":"Cuba Libre (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Cuba Libre is a studio album by Lasse Stefanz, released in 2011. Already before the album was released, the band had sold platinum for the 14th time."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/90/LasseStefanz_CubaL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba_Libre_(album)"},{"title":"Rum and Coke","blocks":[{"text":"Rum and Coke, or the Cuba libre, is a highball cocktail consisting of cola, rum, and in many recipes lime juice on ice. Traditionally, the cola ingredient is Coca-Cola (\"Coke\") and the alcohol is a light rum such as Bacardi; however, the drink may be made with various types of rums and cola brands, and lime juice may or may not be included."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0056.jpg/330px-15-09-26-RalfR-WLC-0056.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rum_and_Coke"},{"title":"Cuba","blocks":[{"text":"Cuba, officially the Republic of Cuba, is an island country in the Caribbean. It comprises the eponymous main island as well as 4,195 islands, islets, and cays. Situated at the convergence of the Caribbean Sea, Gulf of Mexico, and Atlantic Ocean, Cuba is located east of the Yucatán Peninsula, south of both Florida and the Bahamas, west of Hispaniola, and north of Jamaica and the Cayman Islands. Cuba is the largest country in the Caribbean by area and the third-largest by population, after Haiti and the Dominican Republic. Culturally, Cuba is considered to be part of Latin America. Its capital and largest city is Havana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Flag_of_Cuba.svg/330px-Flag_of_Cuba.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cuba"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Cuba_Libre_00.jpg/500px-Cuba_Libre_00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Cuba_Libre_00.jpg/1280px-Cuba_Libre_00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Cuba_Libre_00.jpg/500px-Cuba_Libre_00.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Cuba libre with Coca-Cola and lime","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACuba_Libre_00.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bundyrum24x6cans.JPG/500px-Bundyrum24x6cans.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Bundyrum24x6cans.JPG/500px-Bundyrum24x6cans.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pre-mixed Bundaberg Rum & Cola, 2006","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABundyrum24x6cans.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/DiegoVelazquezCuellar.jpg/500px-DiegoVelazquezCuellar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/DiegoVelazquezCuellar.jpg/1280px-DiegoVelazquezCuellar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/DiegoVelazquezCuellar.jpg/500px-DiegoVelazquezCuellar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diego Velázquez de Cuéllar, conquistador of Cuba","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiegoVelazquezCuellar.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Carlos_Manuel_de_Cespedes.jpg/330px-Carlos_Manuel_de_Cespedes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Carlos_Manuel_de_Cespedes.jpg/330px-Carlos_Manuel_de_Cespedes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Carlos Manuel de Céspedes is known as Father of the Homeland in Cuba, having declared its independence from Spain in 1868. Céspedes was killed by Spanish troops in 1874.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarlos_Manuel_de_Cespedes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Human_remains_in_Cuba.jpg/500px-Human_remains_in_Cuba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Human_remains_in_Cuba.jpg/500px-Human_remains_in_Cuba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Human remains from the Cuban War of Independence after the Spanish reconcentration policy, 1898","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHuman_remains_in_Cuba.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/1933-Pentarchy_w_Batista.jpg/500px-1933-Pentarchy_w_Batista.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/1933-Pentarchy_w_Batista.jpg/500px-1933-Pentarchy_w_Batista.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Pentarchy of 1933. Fulgencio Batista, who controlled the armed forces, appears at far right","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1933-Pentarchy_w_Batista.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/HavanaSlums1954.jpg/500px-HavanaSlums1954.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/HavanaSlums1954.jpg/500px-HavanaSlums1954.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Slum (bohío) dwellings in Havana, Cuba in 1954, just outside Havana baseball stadium. In the background is advertising for a nearby casino.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHavanaSlums1954.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/CheyFidel.jpg/500px-CheyFidel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/CheyFidel.jpg/500px-CheyFidel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Che Guevara and Fidel Castro, photographed by Alberto Korda in 1961","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACheyFidel.jpg"}],"sounds":{"libre":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5c/En-us-Libra.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5c/En-us-Libra.ogg/En-us-Libra.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Churchill House Renovation, December 2022, Brown University","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Churchill_House_Renovation%2C_December_2022%2C_Brown_University.jpg/500px-Churchill_House_Renovation%2C_December_2022%2C_Brown_University.jpg","ratio":1.5880017644464048,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Churchill_House_Renovation,_December_2022,_Brown_University.jpg","share":0.05125},{"title":"The Brown ice resurfacer","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/The_Brown_ice_resurfacer.jpg/500px-The_Brown_ice_resurfacer.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Brown_ice_resurfacer.jpg","share":0.043125}]}}